course: dictionary
lesson: 13779
title: A voice on one note
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone speaks. When you meet one, look at the words around it for clues. «The wizard raised his staff and intoned a spell in a slow, deep voice.» The slow, deep voice is the clue, so intoned must describe a slow way of speaking.
explain: To intone is to say something slowly in a steady, flat voice, almost like singing on one note. It is not loud or excited. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The wizard raised his staff and said a spell in a slow, steady voice» still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Church words often use intone. «The priest intoned the prayer, and the choir answered.» Priests and choirs sing or chant prayers on one note, so intone is the right word there too. The same word can fit a spooky story and a church service.
fact: To intone means to say something slowly in a steady, flat voice.
fact: In church, to intone means to sing or chant the words of a prayer or service on one note.
fact: «The teacher intoned the rules, one by one.» Here it shows a serious, slow voice.
fact: Look for clues such as slow, steady or serious to help you work out what intone means.
fact: Phrases you may meet: intone a prayer, intone the words, intoned solemnly.
exercise: «The priest intoned the prayer, and the choir answered.» What does intoned mean here? | *Said or sang the prayer slowly on one steady note | Shouted it loudly and ran away | Wrote it down on paper | Forgot it completely
exercise: Maya says the teacher intoned the rules. What does this suggest about the teacher's voice? | Bright, fast and cheerful | Quiet, as if whispering a secret | Loud and angry | *Slow, steady and flat, a bit like a song on one note
exercise: «The wizard raised his staff and intoned a spell.» Find and copy the word that tells you how the wizard spoke. | staff | *intoned | raised | spell
test: «The monk intoned the psalm, one long note after another.» What is the best meaning of intoned? | *Sang or chanted on one steady note | Laughed at a joke | Dropped it on the floor | Tore up the page
test: Why might a story say a wizard intones a spell? | To show he is in a hurry and late for dinner | To show he is cold and wants a coat | *To show his voice is slow, serious and a little spooky | To show he has lost his wand
exam: Ben says, «Intone means to shout loudly.» Using the dictionary meaning, is Ben right? | No, it means to write | *No, it means to say something slowly in a steady, flat voice | Yes, it means to shout | Yes, it means to dance
